    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0022" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg12"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 550.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 4, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit a copy of a
                    note addressed by Lord Russell to me on the 27th ultimo, in reply to mine of the
                    3d of the same month, which was written in the sense of your despatch No. 736,
                    of the 17th of October. The ground taken seems to me technically defensible,
                    though a promise of a little investigation or at least close observation at St.
                    George’s would have been more satisfactory than throwing the burden of proof
                    entirely on us.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d5-a1.xml" xpointer="d5-a1"/>
            </div>
